{"id": "988457a63ade1d67ee78ae08cf7c45997cf2fedd", "repo": "cashubtc/orchard", "sha": "988457a63ade1d67ee78ae08cf7c45997cf2fedd", "message": "chore: refuse to publish a release image missing a platform\n\nThe merge job tagged whatever digests it downloaded. If one platform's\ndigest artifact had expired (after 1 day) before someone clicked\n\"Re-run failed jobs\", the release tags and latest got a single-platform\nimage. Fail unless both digests are present, and keep them for the 30\nday re-run window.\n\nAlso lowercase the image name. metadata-action lowercases its own\noutput, but the name also goes straight to buildx and the shell steps.", "authored_at": "2026-10-30T11:24:20Z", "committed_at": "2026-10-30T11:24:20Z", "author_login": "lorenzolfm", "committer_login": "lorenzolfm", "additions": 17, "deletions": 3, "changed_files": 1, "associated_merged_pr_numbers": [223], "url": "https://github.com/cashubtc/orchard/commit/988457a63ade1d67ee78ae08cf7c45997cf2fedd"}
{"id": "a51a486ab5b332090423bfe42688d609ddc96b5b", "repo": "cashubtc/orchard", "sha": "a51a486ab5b332090423bfe42688d609ddc96b5b", "message": "chore: build release images on native arm64 runners\n\nThe v1.12.1 release run never published an image. An arm64 process in\n`RUN npm ci` died with SIGILL under QEMU. npm was PID 1 in the build\ncontainer, and the kernel ignores the signal QEMU re-raises on itself\nfor PID 1, so the job hung until the 6 hour limit.\n\nBuild each platform on its own native runner (ubuntu-24.04 and\nubuntu-24.04-arm), push by digest, then merge the digests into the same\ntags as before. Timeouts make a stuck job fail in an hour.", "authored_at": "2026-10-30T10:27:39Z", "committed_at": "2026-10-30T10:27:39Z", "author_login": "lorenzolfm", "committer_login": "lorenzolfm", "additions": 81, "deletions": 15, "changed_files": 1, "associated_merged_pr_numbers": [223], "url": "https://github.com/cashubtc/orchard/commit/a51a486ab5b332090423bfe42688d609ddc96b5b"}
